 election with a large financial edge, having raised about $5.4 million to Republican John Deaton's $1.6 million, with no outside spending against him.\n\nRecent polls from MassINC and the University of New Hampshire show Markey ahead by 22 to 26 points among likely voters, consistent with averages near 24 points. Deaton, a crypto attorney running as an anti-Trump Republican, faces a skeptical electorate; even supportive coverage describes his path as difficult. All ten expert ratings call the race Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price a Markey win at 98 to 99 percent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9975, "margin": 19.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9987, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9989, "margin": 24.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 24.0}]}